IETF / IANA leap-seconds.list (public domain)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

tests/data/leap-seconds.list is a copy of the leap-second file distributed
with the IANA time zone database, updated through IERS Bulletin C. The file
states: "This file is in the public domain."

------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAIF SPICE leapseconds kernel naif0012.tls (constants only)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/tdb.rs holds the four DELTET constants of the NAIF leapseconds kernel
naif0012.tls (DELTET/K, DELTET/EB and the two DELTET/M values), from the
Navigation and Ancillary Information Facility (NAIF), NASA Jet Propulsion
Laboratory (https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/lsk/). The
kernel file itself is not included; the reference-table generator downloads
it and checks its SHA-256.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
ERFA (Essential Routines for Fundamental Astronomy)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/fb1990_table.rs holds the 787 coefficients of the Fairhead & Bretagnon
(1990) TDB-TT series, and src/leap.rs holds the 1960-1971 TAI-UTC
expressions, both taken from ERFA v2.0.1 (https://github.com/liberfa/erfa,
commit 9915ba38c9365f8b0738269b8c2ac1fdd5f8dee3, files src/dtdb.c and
src/dat.c). The evaluation order of the series follows eraDtdb.
src/iau2006_table.rs holds the IAU 2000A nutation series and the series of
the CIO locator s from the same release (src/nut00a.c and src/s06.c), and
src/frames.rs follows the expressions and evaluation order of eraEra00,
eraGmst82, eraSp00, eraPom00, eraNut00a, eraNut06a, eraPfw06, eraObl06,
eraFw2m, eraPnm06a, eraS06, eraC2ixys, eraC2i06a, eraC2tcio, eraC2t06a and
the eraFa*03 fundamental arguments. ERFA is distributed under the following
